<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77920" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραδιαζευκτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, σύνδεσμος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>subdisjunctive</i>, i. e.
			disjunctive, with the meaning '<i>or if you like</i>', used where
			either alternative alone and the two together are alike admissible,
			e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠέ</span>) in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ νέος ἠὲ
			παλαιός</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.108
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Conj.</u>
				219.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.80
			</span></i>, cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.517
			</span></i>, etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					7.537
				</span></i>
			, al.</div>
